#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:55
msgid ""
"When off (default): the sidebar stays visible, except that it steps aside "
"while a window covers its area (see sidebar-hide-when-covered). When on: the "
"sidebar stays off screen and is revealed by moving the pointer to the screen "
"edge it is attached to."
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:60
msgid "Hide the Sidebar When a Window Covers It"
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:61
msgid ""
"With auto-hide off, the sidebar slides out of the way while a window "
"overlaps its area, so that window stays fully clickable, and comes back once "
"the area is clear, the way macOS Stage Manager does. Move the pointer to the "
"screen edge to reveal it meanwhile. Has no effect while space is reserved "
"for the sidebar, since windows then never cover it."
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:66
msgid "Park the Stage on Desktop Click"
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:67
msgid ""
"In Groups mode, clicking the empty desktop minimizes the current stage into "
"a single card and reveals the wallpaper, as clicking the wallpaper does on "
"macOS."
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:73
msgid ""
"When enabled, always show the sidebar when all windows on the current "
"workspace are minimized (desktop is empty). Auto-hide resumes once the user "
"interacts with a card and windows become visible again."
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:78
msgid "Reserve Space for the Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:79
msgid ""
"Shrink the work area so maximized windows stop underneath the sidebar "
"instead of being covered by it, the way macOS shifts the stage across. Only "
"applies when auto-hide is off, because a reserved strut cannot animate."
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:85
msgid "Auto-hide Delay"
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:86
msgid ""
"Delay in milliseconds before hiding the sidebar after the pointer leaves."
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:93
msgid ""
"Width of the invisible hot zone at the screen edge to trigger the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:100
msgid ""
"How long in milliseconds the pointer must rest on the screen edge before the "
"sidebar appears. Stops the sidebar opening when you brush past the edge on "
"the way to an app's own left-edge UI, such as a vertical tab bar. Set to 0 "
"to open instantly."
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:105
msgid "Show Application Icons"
msgstr ""

#: src/schemas/org.gnome.shell.extensions.stage-manager.gschema.xml:106
